# GovCatalyst — Backend Gap Analysis
**Against the Government Innovation Procurement Problem Statement**

---

## What's Already Built ✅

| Area | What Exists |
|---|---|
| Auth | JWT login/register, OTP activation, super-admin approval flow |
| Startup discovery | DPIIT mock-registry verification, startup profile CRUD |
| Challenge creation | AI-assisted outcome-statement generation (Gemini), tech-tag extraction |
| Application screening | AI proposal scoring (0–100), auto-shortlist at threshold ≥75 |
| Pilot lifecycle | State-machine with 13 states (DRAFT → SCALE/REJECT), security gate |
| Pilot sub-models | KPI, Risk, Issue, Feedback, Evidence, Evaluation DB models |
| Pilot service | KPI improvement calc, cybersecurity 14-point gate, automated outcome engine |
| Document service | 22-section completion report + bilateral agreement generator |
| Audit service | In-memory action log (pilot mutations) |
| Email notifications | Nodemailer — new registrations, OTP, rejections |

---

## Critical Gaps 🚨

### 1. Pilot Routes Not Wired Into Express App
**File:** [`app.js`](file:///c:/Users/tussh/OneDrive/Desktop/govCatalyst/server/src/app.js#L17-L24)

`pilot.routes.js` is defined but **never mounted** in `app.js`. The entire pilot module is unreachable via HTTP.

```js
// Missing from app.js:
const pilotRoutes = require('./routes/pilot.routes');
app.use('/api/pilots', pilotRoutes);
```

Also `pilot.routes.js` imports `auth.middleware` (non-existent file) instead of the actual `authMiddleware.js`, so it would crash on load.

---

### 2. Pilot Controller Uses In-Memory Store — No Database Persistence
**File:** [`pilot.controller.js`](file:///c:/Users/tussh/OneDrive/Desktop/govCatalyst/server/src/controllers/pilot.controller.js#L12-L80)

All pilot data lives in a `let memoryPilots = [...]` array. This means:
- Data is lost on every server restart
- No multi-instance or load-balanced deployment possible
- The Sequelize-based [`pilot.model.js`](file:///c:/Users/tussh/OneDrive/Desktop/govCatalyst/server/src/models/pilot.model.js) exists but is **completely unused**
- Sub-models (`pilotKpi.model.js`, `pilotRisk.model.js`, etc.) exist but are never queried

